  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of IOM Activities in Pakistan Outlined in the 2022 Refugee Response Plan (RRP) for the Afghanistan Situation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan remains the third-largest refugee-hosting country globally, hosting over 1.4 million Afghan refugees holding Proof of Registration (PoR) cards issued by the Government, 840,000 Afghan Citizen Card (ACC) holders, and an estimated 775,000 undocumented Afghan migrants. With the recent unprecedented change in the political and security situation in Afghanistan, the number of Afghan nationals crossing into Pakistan has increased, with this trend projected to continue in the short to medium term. Owing to their partly informal status, the Afghan migrant populations have largely remained under the radar, not being eligible for any systematic humanitarian assistance - thereby facing significant challenges. Through both direct implementation and implementing partners, IOM&apos;s interventions are targeting both vulnerable Afghans and host communities with a multi-sectoral set of activities including livelihood support; improved access to basic services; shelter; protection; and an improved evidence base about Afghan migrants&apos; mobility trends, needs and vulnerabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
